            <ArticleTitle>[Experimental study on the effect of ginkgo bioba extract on the expression of heme oxygenase-1 in bronchial asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>302-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To explore the effect of the ginkgo bioba extract on the expression of heme oxygenase-1 (HO-1) in bronchial asthma.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">30 guinea pigs were randomly divided into 3 groups (n = 10): (1) Normal control group; (2) Asthmatic group; (3) Therapeutic group. Blood carbon monoxide Hb (COHb) percent value, Airway resistance and eosinophilic inflammation of airway wall were observed, the expression of HO-1 in lung tissue were observed by immunohistochemical staining.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The expression of HO-1 was mainly located in airway epithelium in these 3 groups, the optical densities were 0.170 +/- 0.020, 0.707 +/- 0.058, 0.397 +/- 0.034, respectively. The asthmatic group showed higher optical densities than that of the normal control group (P &lt; 0.01), and the therapeutic group showed lower optical density than asthmatic group (P &lt; 0.01).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The expression of HO-1 is inhibited significantly by the treatment of the ginkgo bioba extract, which may be one of the mechanism for treating asthma by ginkgo bioba extract.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
